From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SteamOS-ARM-RM6 <exclaim_plethora227@simplelogin.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 19:30:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: nx669j: CPU capacity and energy model

sm8350.dtsi has no capacity-dmips-mhz or dynamic-power-coefficient (the
SM8250, SM8550 and SM8650 ones do), so every CPU reports cpu_capacity
1024: the scheduler treats the four Cortex-A55s like the A78s and the X1,
places game threads on them just as readily, and there is no energy model
for energy-aware scheduling. konkrd's big-core boost also found no big
cores and pinned games to all eight.

Take the values from Nubia's stock Lahaina DTB: A55 1024/100, A78
1946/499, X1 2048/760.

---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8350-nubia-nx669j.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8350-nubia-nx669j.dts
@@ -619,6 +619,52 @@
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
+/*
+ * CPU capacity and energy model, from Nubia's stock Lahaina DTB (sm8350.dtsi
+ * has neither). Without them the scheduler sees eight equal CPUs
+ * (cpu_capacity 1024 everywhere): game threads land on the A55s as readily
+ * as on the X1, and schedutil gets no energy-aware placement.
+ */
+&cpu0 {
+	capacity-dmips-mhz = <1024>;
+	dynamic-power-coefficient = <100>;
+};
+
+&cpu1 {
+	capacity-dmips-mhz = <1024>;
+	dynamic-power-coefficient = <100>;
+};
+
+&cpu2 {
+	capacity-dmips-mhz = <1024>;
+	dynamic-power-coefficient = <100>;
+};
+
+&cpu3 {
+	capacity-dmips-mhz = <1024>;
+	dynamic-power-coefficient = <100>;
+};
+
+&cpu4 {
+	capacity-dmips-mhz = <1946>;
+	dynamic-power-coefficient = <499>;
+};
+
+&cpu5 {
+	capacity-dmips-mhz = <1946>;
+	dynamic-power-coefficient = <499>;
+};
+
+&cpu6 {
+	capacity-dmips-mhz = <1946>;
+	dynamic-power-coefficient = <499>;
+};
+
+&cpu7 {
+	capacity-dmips-mhz = <2048>;
+	dynamic-power-coefficient = <760>;
+};
+
 &gpi_dma0 {
 	status = "okay";
 };
